infographic sequence-snake-steps-underline-text
data
  title SameSite: trading CSRF protection for cross-site reach
  desc Each step down sends the cookie on more cross-site requests — more functionality, less CSRF defence. Lax is the modern browser default when the directive is absent.
  sequences
    - label Strict — never cross-site
      desc Cookie is withheld on every cross-site request, including top-level navigations from a link. Strongest CSRF defence; can log a user out when they arrive from an external link.
    - label Lax — safe navigations only (default)
      desc Sent on safe cross-site navigations (following a link) but not on cross-site POST/PUT. Blocks most CSRF while keeping link-in flows working. Browsers apply this when SameSite is absent.
    - label None; Secure — all cross-site
      desc Sent on every cross-site request, so it must pair with Secure. Needed for legitimate third-party embeds, but offers no SameSite CSRF protection — pair with a CSRF token.
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f59e0b #f43f5e
